<title>FRANCE: Cr. Lyonnais soar on govt rescue hopes.</title>
<headline>Cr. Lyonnais soar on govt rescue hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ailing bank Credit Lyonnais were up sharply on Friday on hopes that the French government was close to agreeing a new rescue plan for the state-owned bank, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1112 GMT, its shares had climbed 20.1 francs or 16 percent to 133.10 while the blue chip CAC-40 market was down 0.51 percent.</p>
<p>Reports say that under the latest salvage scheme, most of the heavy costs imposed on the bank as part of its state bailout last year would likely be waived.</p>
</text>
